1
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,860
On Saturday, 3 January 2026, United States
forces captured Venezuela's president,

2
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:19,400
Nicolás Maduro, in Caracas
and took him to New York.

3
00:00:19,952 --> 00:00:22,457
Two days later, in a federal
courtroom in Manhattan,

4
00:00:22,817 --> 00:00:23,697
he pleaded not guilty.

5
00:00:24,284 --> 00:00:26,844
He is accused, and he has not
been convicted of anything.

6
00:00:27,455 --> 00:00:30,200
This is the story of how a
bus driver became a president,

7
00:00:30,580 --> 00:00:33,420
and of what voters, observers and
courts have said about it since.

8
00:00:34,117 --> 00:00:38,557
Nicolás Maduro was born in
Caracas on 23 November 1962.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,045
He worked for years as a bus
driver on the Caracas Metro,

10
00:00:42,545 --> 00:00:43,925
and became a trade union leader.

11
00:00:44,529 --> 00:00:48,094
In 1992 he campaigned for
the release of Hugo Chávez,

12
00:00:48,834 --> 00:00:51,574
an army officer jailed
after a failed coup attempt.

13
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:56,040
Chávez was elected president in
1998, and Maduro rose with him:

14
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:00,580
a member of the National Assembly
from 2000, its president in 2005,

15
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,100
and foreign minister from 2006.

16
00:01:03,896 --> 00:01:06,821
In October 2012 Chávez
made him vice president,

17
00:01:07,241 --> 00:01:09,921
and Chávez died on 5 March 2013.

18
00:01:10,669 --> 00:01:16,704
Maduro took over as acting president, and
the election was held on 14 April 2013.

19
00:01:17,443 --> 00:01:23,683
According to the national electoral council,
he won by 50.6 percent to 49.1 percent,

20
00:01:24,123 --> 00:01:27,263
a margin of about two hundred
and twenty-four thousand votes.

21
00:01:27,910 --> 00:01:32,975
His opponent, Henrique Capriles, refused to
concede and listed more than three thousand

22
00:01:32,975 --> 00:01:33,695
irregularities.

23
00:01:34,618 --> 00:01:38,733
The council audited the remaining ballots
and said in June that the result stood,

24
00:01:39,153 --> 00:01:42,053
and the Supreme Court rejected
Capriles's appeal in August.

25
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:51,013
Five years later, the argument
was no longer about a margin.

26
00:01:51,613 --> 00:01:53,453
It was about who was allowed to run.

27
00:01:54,047 --> 00:01:58,692
The vote of 20 May 2018 was boycotted
by the main opposition coalition,

28
00:01:59,072 --> 00:02:02,292
and several leading opposition
figures were barred or jailed.

29
00:02:02,859 --> 00:02:06,724
The electoral council said
Maduro won with 67.8 percent,

30
00:02:06,824 --> 00:02:08,864
on a turnout of about 46 percent.

31
00:02:09,323 --> 00:02:13,528
The European Union, the United States and
the Lima Group of Latin American governments

32
00:02:13,528 --> 00:02:15,288
did not recognise the result.

33
00:02:16,108 --> 00:02:17,768
Russia, China and others did.

34
00:02:18,324 --> 00:02:20,829
Maduro's government said
the vote followed the rules,

35
00:02:21,249 --> 00:02:22,589
and rejected the foreign criticism.

36
00:02:23,265 --> 00:02:27,665
The next presidential election
was held on 28 July 2024.

37
00:02:28,355 --> 00:02:31,155
The next day, the council
announced that Maduro had won,

38
00:02:31,635 --> 00:02:37,375
with 51.2 percent against 44.2
percent for Edmundo González Urrutia,

39
00:02:37,855 --> 00:02:42,875
a former diplomat who stood after the government
barred the opposition leader María Corina Machado.

40
00:02:43,492 --> 00:02:47,097
The council did not publish results
from the individual polling stations.

41
00:02:47,764 --> 00:02:50,864
The opposition collected printed
tally sheets from the voting machines,

42
00:02:51,084 --> 00:02:56,544
put them online, and said they showed González
with about 67 percent and Maduro with about 30.

43
00:02:57,130 --> 00:02:59,710
The Carter Center, which had
a small team on the ground,

44
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:03,870
said the election did not meet international
standards of electoral integrity,

45
00:03:04,230 --> 00:03:06,270
and that it could not
verify the official result.

46
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:11,973
A panel of United Nations electoral experts said
that announcing a winner before polling-station

47
00:03:11,973 --> 00:03:16,173
results existed had no precedent in
contemporary democratic elections.

48
00:03:16,851 --> 00:03:20,596
The government said the count was correct and
that its system had suffered a cyberattack,

49
00:03:21,196 --> 00:03:26,156
and on 22 August the Supreme Tribunal of
Justice confirmed Maduro as the winner.

50
00:03:32,067 --> 00:03:35,287
While the elections were argued
over, the economy was falling apart.

51
00:03:35,802 --> 00:03:39,002
Venezuela has the largest proven
oil reserves in the world,

52
00:03:39,162 --> 00:03:47,302
but its oil output fell from about 2.7 million
barrels a day in 2013 to about one million in 2025.

53
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:52,450
The Congressional Research Service says the
economy contracted by more than seventy-five

54
00:03:52,450 --> 00:03:55,790
percent between 2013 and 2021.

55
00:03:56,654 --> 00:04:00,999
Prices rose out of control, and shops and
hospitals ran short of food and medicine.

56
00:04:01,671 --> 00:04:06,596
Maduro's government blamed American
sanctions and what it called an economic war.

57
00:04:07,132 --> 00:04:11,717
By 2024, about seventy-three percent
of Venezuelans lived in poverty,

58
00:04:12,117 --> 00:04:15,337
according to a survey by the
Andrés Bello Catholic University.

59
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:22,760
And millions left. By December 2024, United
Nations agencies counted about 7.9 million

60
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:27,500
Venezuelan refugees and migrants abroad,
roughly one in four of the country's people.

61
00:04:28,115 --> 00:04:30,720
Most of them stayed in Latin
America and the Caribbean.

62
00:04:43,267 --> 00:04:48,967
A United Nations fact-finding mission reported
that since 2019 security forces had arbitrarily

63
00:04:48,967 --> 00:04:52,247
detained, tortured and killed
opponents of the government.

64
00:04:52,857 --> 00:04:54,577
The government rejected those findings.

65
00:05:00,628 --> 00:05:03,513
In New York, prosecutors
had been building a case.

66
00:05:04,157 --> 00:05:10,997
On 26 March 2020, Attorney General William Barr
announced narco-terrorism and drug trafficking

67
00:05:10,997 --> 00:05:14,037
charges against Maduro and
other Venezuelan officials.

68
00:05:14,819 --> 00:05:18,324
Prosecutors alleged that he led a
network called the Cartel of the Suns,

69
00:05:18,924 --> 00:05:22,244
and worked with Colombian guerrillas
to move cocaine to the United States.

70
00:05:22,984 --> 00:05:26,784
The State Department offered a
reward of up to 15 million dollars,

71
00:05:27,044 --> 00:05:29,924
which it raised to 50
million in August 2025.

72
00:05:30,782 --> 00:05:35,082
Maduro answered that the United States and
Colombia were conspiring against Venezuela.

73
00:05:35,767 --> 00:05:41,612
In September 2025 the United States began
strikes on boats it said were carrying drugs,

74
00:05:41,872 --> 00:05:46,552
and in November it named the Cartel of
the Suns a foreign terrorist organisation.

75
00:05:47,382 --> 00:05:53,267
On 3 January 2026, President Donald Trump
announced that American forces had carried

76
00:05:53,267 --> 00:05:56,207
out an operation in Caracas
to bring Maduro to justice.

77
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:30,640
Delcy Rodríguez, Maduro's vice president,
first called him the only legitimate president,

78
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:35,020
and then became acting president and
offered to cooperate with Washington.

79
00:06:45,433 --> 00:06:49,153
A new indictment, unsealed that
day, charged Maduro and his wife,

80
00:06:49,413 --> 00:06:52,213
Cilia Flores, with
narco-terrorism conspiracy,

81
00:06:52,833 --> 00:06:55,673
cocaine importation conspiracy
and weapons offences.

82
00:06:56,408 --> 00:06:59,833
The Justice Department states that
an indictment is only an accusation,

83
00:07:00,453 --> 00:07:03,633
and that the defendants are presumed
innocent unless proven guilty.

84
00:07:04,295 --> 00:07:08,380
In October prosecutors added a charge
of conspiracy to commit torture.

85
00:07:09,020 --> 00:07:11,140
Both defendants have pleaded not guilty.

86
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:15,040
The defence says that, as a head
of state, Maduro has immunity,

87
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,920
and that his capture was unlawful.

88
00:07:17,660 --> 00:07:20,240
In November it asked the
court to dismiss the case.

89
00:07:21,140 --> 00:07:22,480
Prosecutors oppose both arguments.

90
00:07:23,174 --> 00:07:28,699
Judge Alvin Hellerstein died on 28 October,
and the case passed to Judge Analisa Torres,

91
00:07:28,979 --> 00:07:32,679
who kept the schedule: a hearing
on those motions on 17 December,

92
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:36,219
and a trial date of 14 June 2027.

93
00:07:36,818 --> 00:07:39,958
Maduro is held at the Metropolitan
Detention Center in Brooklyn.

94
00:07:40,612 --> 00:07:43,397
In Caracas, Rodríguez
remains acting president.

95
00:07:44,237 --> 00:07:47,597
Her government passed an amnesty law
and freed some political prisoners,

96
00:07:48,037 --> 00:07:50,537
and Washington lifted its
sanctions on her in April.

97
00:07:51,145 --> 00:07:54,885
Machado, who received the Nobel
Peace Prize in December 2025,

98
00:07:55,325 --> 00:07:59,785
came back to Venezuela on 25
October after ten months in exile.

99
00:08:01,005 --> 00:08:03,605
González, who lives in Madrid,
has said he will follow.

100
00:08:04,485 --> 00:08:08,025
Talks between the government and the
opposition began in August, without her.

101
00:08:08,483 --> 00:08:10,368
The elections were judged by observers.

102
00:08:11,228 --> 00:08:13,288
The charges will be judged by a jury.

103
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:17,690
No court has decided yet. What
would you want proven first?
